# EXPECT: rebinds it to a bool
#
# #1637 (EigenScript#1647): `p` is a C double in g (its body compares it
# with a number, which is numeric evidence), and `p is p > 3` rebinds it to
# a bool. The VM runs this (rc 0, prints true then false). Before the bool
# type the comparison was a number and this compiled; now the AOT refuses
# it by name at build time instead of compiling a runtime death -- the same
# class as rebinding a numeric parameter to null or a string.
define g(p) as:
    p is p > 3
    return p
print of (g of 5)
print of (g of 1)
